WEBVTT

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.850
<i>It's already been a week since then.</i>

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:06.730
<i>Fukami-san has invited me numerous times...</i>

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:08.190
I finally caught you!

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.740
Why haven't you been coming here lately?

00:00:10.740 --> 00:00:11.820
I've been waiting for you!

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:14.780
It felt great, didn't it?

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.340
Did you forget that already?

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:18.410
It was your first time, wasn't it?

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:21.500
Anyone would want to keep doing it more...

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.500
after getting a correct answer 
like that in quiz bowl!

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.120
It's not so much quiz bowl...

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.130
I haven't really given much 
thought to any clubs yet.

00:00:33.610 --> 00:00:35.740
If you haven't picked one, that's perfect!

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:37.470
You can't just run away now! It's not fair!

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:40.220
Yeah, but...

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:46.650
Koshiyama-kun...

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:49.860
Listen to me, okay?

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:50.610
O-Okay...

00:00:51.810 --> 00:00:54.030
Tomorrow is Saturday, 
and we don't have school.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:55.450
Will you be free?

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:58.510
Huh? W-Well, if I had to say 
one way or the other...

00:00:58.510 --> 00:00:59.580
I-I'm free, yes.

00:01:00.050 --> 00:01:01.880
Then I'll be waiting 
tomorrow morning at ten,

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:04.040
at the Kawata Station ticket gates.

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.540
Huh?! Wh-Wh-Why?!

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:08.610
Fukami-san, you're proposing a date already?

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:09.620
With <i>him</i>?

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:10.500
Huh?

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:13.800
N-No, it's not like that!

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:17.830
There's a quiz meet tomorrow 
at Sekigaoka High School.

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:20.010
Our quiz bowl circle is going to watch!

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.140
Huh?

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:25.600
I want you to watch it with us, 
even if it's only as a provisional member.

00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:28.010
O-Oh, a quiz thing?

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:29.400
I see... A quiz thing...

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.770
Um, Fukami-san...

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:34.410
Could I join you for that, too?

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:35.110
Really?

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:38.030
Yes! Please come along, Inoue-kun!

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:43.990
Koshiyama-kun, see you tomorrow!

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:47.000
Uh, yeah. Tomorrow.

00:02:05.350 --> 00:02:10.310
<b>Fastest Finger First</b>

00:03:16.960 --> 00:03:20.920
<b>Question 2: "A Matter of 0.01 Seconds?!"</b>

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:25.890
<i>I let her talk me into coming,</i>

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:29.780
<i>but doesn't getting here first make 
me look like I'm trying too hard?</i>

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:30.990
Koshiyama-kun!

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:37.220
I'm so glad! You really came!

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.650
I was kind of pushy about it, 
so I was worried you wouldn't.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.250
Still twenty minutes to go...

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.080
<i>Wait, am I alone with Fukami-san right now?</i>

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:53.790
<i>I'm alone with a girl, 
even though I'm not at school?</i>

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.790
<i>Wh-What do I talk about?</i>

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:57.480
Okay, here's a question.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:58.130
Huh?

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:02.810
Napoleon was famously born on what 
Mediterranean island in the French domain?

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:04.090
Corsica?

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:05.050
Bingo!

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:07.510
<i>She's quizzing me here?</i>

00:04:07.770 --> 00:04:10.240
So you're good with history too, huh?

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:11.980
Y-Yeah, sort of...

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:14.940
Then... how about questions like this?

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:17.190
Here.

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:23.240
The area of exposed skin 
between the hem of a miniskirt

00:04:23.240 --> 00:04:27.070
and the tops of knee-high 
socks is known by what name?

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:29.540
Th-There's a name for that?

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.540
As I suspected.

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:35.230
You like books, but you're not an otaku.

00:04:35.230 --> 00:04:36.500
Wh-What's the answer?

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.960
Absolute territory.

00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:42.340
Absolute... territory?

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:45.000
You know how guys like a teasing 
hint more than full nudity?

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:49.600
In certain circles, it's one of the 
most potent aspects of moe culture.

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:51.600
I had no idea...

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:53.810
Absolute territory...

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:54.600
You won't find it.

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:59.980
The way you crave more knowledge makes 
you even more suited for quiz bowl.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:02.240
S-Straight to that topic again...

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:06.340
Exchanging quiz questions and answers 
with others is fun, isn't it?

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:10.350
I played with my friend that way 
in middle school all the time.

00:05:10.350 --> 00:05:11.080
Your friend?

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:13.240
Yeah.

00:05:14.610 --> 00:05:17.450
We ended up in different 
high schools, though.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.590
I hope we can do quiz bowl 
together again someday.

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:24.050
<i>A friend who shares the same hobby, huh?</i>

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.980
Maybe I should've joined 
the literature club.

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:29.010
Wait!

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:31.550
Don't make that your answer yet!

00:05:31.550 --> 00:05:33.350
At least not until after today's meet!

00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:38.350
I'll try really hard today, 
so be sure to watch!

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.010
O-Okay.

00:05:42.110 --> 00:05:42.980
Koshiyama!

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:45.610
Man, why did you have to get here so early?!

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:47.450
Damn it! I'm too late!

00:05:47.870 --> 00:05:49.200
Morning, Inoue-kun.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:53.660
Oh. He's from "certain circles."

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.450
Your skirt length, absolute territory,

00:05:56.450 --> 00:06:00.370
and sock length have a 
ratio of 4 to 1 to 2.4.

00:06:00.370 --> 00:06:01.920
That is imperfect, Fukami-kun.

00:06:02.290 --> 00:06:04.300
Good morning, Sasajima-senpai.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:07.840
Incidentally, why are there 
only two of you here?

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:10.030
I'm certain my speech was perfect.

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:11.620
U-Um...

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.260
Oh, you're here?

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:16.150
Um, where are the other circle members?

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:17.910
These are all the members.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:21.230
The Buzou High School quiz 
circle only just started up.

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:23.690
<i>If they don't have enough members,</i>

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:25.640
<i>it's no wonder she wants me to join.</i>

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:28.740
Sekigawata Middle School 
Sekigawata High School

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:28.580
Today's event is a quiz meet hosted by

00:06:28.580 --> 00:06:30.610
the Sekigawata quiz circle for 
new quiz bowl team members.

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:32.040
At other schools,

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:35.080
there may well be students who were interested 
in quiz bowl before the school year began.

00:06:35.740 --> 00:06:37.910
Even if we can't act, you must stay focused.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.870
Um, we're just here to observe, right?

00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:43.130
I've entered all of you.

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:45.200
What?!

00:06:45.200 --> 00:06:46.060
Sorry!

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:47.420
Listen up!

00:06:47.820 --> 00:06:50.090
All those here are both comrades and rivals!

00:06:51.990 --> 00:06:56.610
Be especially attentive to the 
way they all play the game.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:07.190
Our rivals' life bars seem 
to have dropped to zero.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:08.650
Sasajima!

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:11.690
You got enough members. Congrats.

00:07:11.690 --> 00:07:12.610
Niina-san.

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:14.300
Thanks for having us today.

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:17.620
<b>Miyaura High School Third-year
Ashiya Yousuke</b>

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:17.620
<b>Sekigawata High School Third-year 
Niina Takumi</b>

00:07:14.920 --> 00:07:17.620
Wow, I'm jealous. You have a girl member.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:20.580
It makes no difference whether you're 
male or female in quiz bowl.

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:22.870
The reason there are so 
few girls in quiz bowl

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:26.440
is because most of the schools with strong 
quiz bowl teams are all boys' schools.

00:07:26.440 --> 00:07:30.340
But our quiz bowl team is 100% female.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:30.340
<b>Asagaoka Girls' High School Third-year
Sonohara Chiaki</b>

00:07:30.810 --> 00:07:32.800
Welcome, Chiaki-san.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:35.060
An all-girls school quiz bowl team?

00:07:35.060 --> 00:07:36.350
Yukicchi...

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:39.220
Maririn.

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:42.660
I haven't seen you since we graduated.

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:44.940
The Asagaoka uniform looks great on you.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:46.330
Maririn...

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:49.000
I didn't know Buzou had a quiz bowl team.

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:49.900
That's great.

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:53.460
I'm so glad I get to play 
quiz bowl with you again.

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:55.930
Yeah. Good luck to us both.

00:08:00.690 --> 00:08:03.830
<i>Was that the friend from middle school?</i>

00:08:03.830 --> 00:08:05.540
<b>Four Schools Quiz Meet</b>

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:10.920
May the best team win.

00:08:10.920 --> 00:08:11.940
<i>It's starting.</i>

00:08:13.600 --> 00:08:15.430
Here's our program for today.

00:08:15.430 --> 00:08:17.600
The buzzer battle will last three rounds.

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:19.350
<b>Round 1</b>

00:08:18.070 --> 00:08:23.080
In round 1, the 16 participants will 
be split into two groups of eight.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:27.110
<b>Round 2</b>

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:26.690
The three winners in each group 
will proceed to round 2.

00:08:26.690 --> 00:08:29.960
In round 1, the first 
to score 5 points wins.

00:08:28.980 --> 00:08:33.990
<b>First to 5 Points Wins</b>

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:32.020
There's no penalty for an incorrect answer.

00:08:29.980 --> 00:08:33.990
<b>Incorrect Answers: No Penalty</b>

00:08:32.020 --> 00:08:35.570
After buzzing in, you'll have 
five seconds to answer.

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:35.570
<b>Time Limit</b>

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:35.570
<b>Seconds</b>

00:08:35.940 --> 00:08:37.950
We'll start with group 1.

00:08:39.760 --> 00:08:41.080
<i>Yukicchi...</i>

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:43.580
First, we'll have a buzzer test.

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:45.540
A buzzer test?

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:00.180
Wow, that's kinda cool.

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:04.660
The buzzer test verifies that 
all the buzzers are working,

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:07.890
and gives the players a 
feel for the buzzers.

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:10.820
It's an indispensable ritual 
conducted before every match.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:14.360
It can also be called the 
signal to begin the match.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:17.040
<i>W-Will I be doing that, too?</i>

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:19.070
Question.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:22.500
In soccer, games played on a team's 
own field are called "hom—

00:09:23.200 --> 00:09:24.580
<i>A few of them buzzed at once!</i>

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:25.080
<i>But...</i>

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.460
Sasaki-kun.

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:28.330
Away.

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:29.290
Correct!

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:31.170
<i>Fukami-san was beaten to the buzzer...</i>

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.630
Sekigawata Middle School
Sasaki

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:33.630
That Sekigawata Middle 
School first-year is good.

00:09:33.800 --> 00:09:34.840
<i>Middle school first-year?!</i>

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:36.950
In combined middle and high schools,

00:09:36.950 --> 00:09:39.370
many clubs include members 
from both school levels.

00:09:39.920 --> 00:09:42.310
He has an advantage over people 
who start in high school.

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.730
1R  First to 5 Points  Group 1

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.730
Miyaura High School
Mukai

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.730
Sekigawata High School 
Namiki

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.730
Sekigawata High School 
Taguchi

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.730
Miyaura High School 
Maruyama

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.730
Sekigawata Middle School 
Sasaki

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.730
Asagaoka Girls' High School 
Kouzuki

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.730
Buzou High School 
Fukami

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.730
Miyaura High School 
Hamada

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:46.730
Sasaki-kun of Sekigawata Middle School

00:09:46.730 --> 00:09:49.020
passes the round with five points!

00:09:49.320 --> 00:09:51.980
Fukami-san was buzzing in, but...

00:09:52.180 --> 00:09:55.690
Fast buzzing can determine the winner 
by a margin of 0.01 seconds.

00:09:56.440 --> 00:09:59.450
So this is what she meant by 
a margin of 0.01 seconds.

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:03.760
One of the techniques for buzzing 
in at least 0.01 seconds faster

00:10:03.760 --> 00:10:05.200
is called "pushing in."

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:05.910
Pushing in?

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:12.130
Play

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:14.130
Conducting Part

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:11.660
In every buzzer is a contact point and a 
conducting part that makes the light go on,

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:14.130
and the slight gap between 
them is called the "play."

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:19.280
Pushing the button down in advance 
until just before it closes that gap

00:10:19.280 --> 00:10:20.840
is "pushing in."

00:10:21.260 --> 00:10:23.660
I bet I'd accidentally 
push it all the way down.

00:10:24.100 --> 00:10:24.810
Me, too.

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:29.610
<i>Fukami-san...</i>

00:10:30.920 --> 00:10:31.680
Question.

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:35.280
French for "hide the heart—

00:10:35.710 --> 00:10:36.570
<i>It turned on!</i>

00:10:36.940 --> 00:10:37.880
Cache-cœur.

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:38.820
Correct.

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:40.450
Sekigawata Middle School
Sasaki

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:40.450
Asagaoka Girls' High School 
Kouzuki

00:10:38.820 --> 00:10:40.450
Buzou High School 
Fukami

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:41.670
Question.

00:10:42.170 --> 00:10:45.400
When, even in an economic slump, 
the cost of living continues to rise—

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:47.060
Stagflation.

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:48.120
Correct.

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:50.120
<i>She's hanging in there, too!</i>

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:51.180
Question.

00:10:51.180 --> 00:10:53.310
"Oh! Susanna" and "Camptown Rac—

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:54.750
Foster.

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:56.250
<b>"Oh! Susanna" and "Camptown Races" were written by 
which songwriter, known as the "father of American music"?</b>

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:56.020
Correct.

00:10:57.480 --> 00:11:00.800
Fukami-san of Buzou High School 
passes the round with five points!

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:03.260
Yukicchi...

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:05.260
I'll be waiting for you in round 2.

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:10.480
They're all amazing. 
Can I really do that, too?

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:13.690
I could buzz in even faster.

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:19.530
I can't believe you're so surprised 
by weak buzz-ins like that.

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:21.490
Wha... Who are you?

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:23.990
Huh? Who are <i>you</i>?

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:26.990
<i>What's with this guy?!</i>

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:29.000
I'll wear
this tomorrow...
I guess...

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:31.000
We're the
same height.

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:31.000
No, we're not!

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:31.000
Whoosh       Whoosh

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.600
What middle school are you from, anyway?

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:36.840
Stop it, Mikuriya.

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:38.990
That's rude. Take a good look.

00:11:38.990 --> 00:11:41.330
He's small, but he's in a Buzou uniform.

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:43.120
He's a first-year, like you.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:44.860
Huh? Seriously?!

00:11:44.860 --> 00:11:46.470
Uh, sorry.

00:11:46.470 --> 00:11:47.260
It's okay...

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:49.680
Asagaoka Girls' High School
Kouzuki

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:50.140
Correct!

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:51.230
Sekigawata Middle School
Sasaki

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:51.230
Buzou High School 
Fukami

00:11:49.680 --> 00:11:50.430
Asagaoka Girls' High School
Kouzuki

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:53.590
Kouzuki-san of Asagaoka Girls' 
High School has passed the round!

00:11:55.090 --> 00:11:57.520
<i>That's the way, Yukicchi.</i>

00:11:57.770 --> 00:12:00.360
And now we have our three advancers.

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:02.170
That's the end of the first group.

00:12:02.170 --> 00:12:05.320
Sasajima-senpai, how was my buzzing?

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:06.490
Not bad.

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:10.210
You seem to excel at classics, 
but that won't be enough.

00:12:10.720 --> 00:12:13.460
The second round is sure to be harder.

00:12:13.740 --> 00:12:16.170
Um... What are "classics"?

00:12:18.490 --> 00:12:20.010
I want to know that, too.

00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:24.570
They're also known as fundamental 
or tired questions.

00:12:25.160 --> 00:12:29.140
They're questions that frequently appear 
in quiz meets and question collections.

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:30.030
Huh?

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:31.650
Oh, I get it.

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:33.130
No, you don't.

00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:36.060
They may be common questions, 
but they'd be hard for you two.

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:39.820
The crux of fast buzzing 
is how quickly you can

00:12:39.820 --> 00:12:43.110
narrow down an answer using every 
word of the question as hints.

00:12:43.490 --> 00:12:46.620
<i>Right... The marks she had 
made on her question sheet!</i>

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:49.270
But the earlier in the meet you are,

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:51.580
The _____ of _____ is _____, but 
the _____ of _____ / is what?

00:12:49.270 --> 00:12:51.770
the more likely you are to get classic 
questions with simple construction.

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:56.380
Which means the more possible patterns 
you know, the greater your advantage.

00:12:52.660 --> 00:12:56.080
The _____ are _____,
__ / ___ and what?

00:12:56.760 --> 00:12:58.210
If you don't know the pattern,

00:12:57.170 --> 00:13:00.090
From the _____ word for _____, / a 
_____ _____ is known by what name?

00:12:58.210 --> 00:13:00.130
you can't choose the right point 
in the question to buzz in.

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:05.380
And all of the most common 
questions start out the same way.

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:06.970
H-Hang on!

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:09.350
This is way too much to take in so soon.

00:13:09.650 --> 00:13:11.970
You're right. Sorry.

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:16.730
To summarize, the first thing to do 
in quiz bowl is memorize the classics.

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:22.950
<i>We don't know the classics at all.</i>

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:25.200
<i>Aren't we at a huge disadvantage here?</i>

00:13:27.260 --> 00:13:30.030
Okay, let's do the buzzer test.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:36.280
<i>Here it comes!</i>

00:13:41.490 --> 00:13:43.340
You pressed it too soon.

00:13:43.530 --> 00:13:46.580
There's no need to rush. Go ahead.

00:13:50.040 --> 00:13:51.390
<i>He sighed?!</i>

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:53.850
<i>Might as well get this over with fast.</i>

00:13:54.410 --> 00:13:55.180
Question.

00:13:56.110 --> 00:13:57.440
When asked, "Why climb—

00:13:57.730 --> 00:13:59.090
Mallory?

00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:00.310
Correct.

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:03.530
<i>That was fast! He almost 
got it just from "why"!</i>

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:08.230
Wow, we started off with one of the 
most overused questions of all, huh?

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:10.980
When asked, "Why climb the mountain?",

00:14:10.980 --> 00:14:15.500
which English mountaineer 
answered, "Because it's there"?

00:14:15.940 --> 00:14:18.730
As soon as you hear "Why climb," 
you know it's George Mallory.

00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:21.250
Remember that, everyone!

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:23.500
That's beyond overused. It's almost scripted.

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:27.210
<i>What kind of quiz bowl insider info is that?</i>

00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:29.470
<i>Still, he got the correct answer.</i>

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:30.440
Question.

00:14:29.470 --> 00:14:32.430
Miyaura High School 
Mikuriya

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:33.250
Officially known as the 
"Convention on Wetlands—

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:35.060
The Ramsar Convention.

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:36.080
Correct.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:37.250
Question.

00:14:37.710 --> 00:14:39.140
"The Congress Dances"—

00:14:39.950 --> 00:14:41.300
The Vienna Congress.

00:14:41.300 --> 00:14:42.200
Correct.

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:43.320
Question.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:45.410
In jazz music, "doo-bee-doo-bee" and—

00:14:45.970 --> 00:14:46.860
Scat?

00:14:47.550 --> 00:14:48.760
Correct!

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:49.830
Question.

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:53.430
In euro, the currency of the 
European Union, the highest—

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:55.790
500 euro.

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:57.250
Correct!

00:14:57.250 --> 00:15:01.920
Mikuriya-kun of Miyaura High School passes 
the first round after the first five questions!

00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:04.670
He's so good, it's creepy.

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:09.270
<i>The official name of the Ramsar Convention is</i>

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:14.480
<i>the "Convention on Wetlands of International 
Importance Especially as Waterfowl Habitat."</i>

00:15:14.480 --> 00:15:17.540
<i>He buzzed in after "Convention on Wetlands."</i>

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:21.730
<i>Were all those other questions classics 
like the "why climb" one, too?</i>

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:25.600
<i>If I know the answer, but can't buzz 
because I don't know the question...</i>

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:28.920
He was pretty bold with his buzzer.

00:15:28.920 --> 00:15:31.150
He buzzed slightly before 
the determining point.

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:33.780
It's a tactic worth using as 
long as there's no penalty.

00:15:34.110 --> 00:15:37.340
<i>With Mikuriya through, 
there are two spots left.</i>

00:15:38.110 --> 00:15:39.180
Question.

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:42.790
In the popular idol group, 
Planet, the oldest—

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:46.710
It lit up! Mirai-can!

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:48.750
C-Correct!

00:15:48.750 --> 00:15:51.260
<i>I-I don't know anything about that stuff!</i>

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:54.940
Um, for what it's worth, 
the buttons are delicate,

00:15:54.940 --> 00:15:56.760
so please use them carefully.

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:57.580
Question.

00:15:58.050 --> 00:16:03.230
Italian for "in the manner of the chapel," 
music with no instrumental—

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:04.400
<i>They got it.</i>

00:16:04.960 --> 00:16:06.050
A cappella.

00:16:06.050 --> 00:16:07.050
Correct.

00:16:08.330 --> 00:16:09.380
<i>This is no good.</i>

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:11.970
<i>I have to be able to buzz at 
the start of the question.</i>

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:12.770
Question.

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:18.240
Newton's three laws are the law of 
inertia, the law of motion, and—

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:23.760
<i>This is just like that question I had 
before about the Kyoto festivals.</i>

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:26.500
The law of action and reaction.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:28.460
Koshiyama

00:16:27.470 --> 00:16:28.460
Correct.

00:16:28.790 --> 00:16:30.440
Wow, nice going.

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:32.140
<i>No, that's not enough!</i>

00:16:32.140 --> 00:16:36.520
<i>The determining point where I buzzed was 
the first syllable of "law of motion."</i>

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:38.470
<i>I need to be faster.</i>

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:49.270
Sekigawata High School
Takamura

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:49.270
Sekigawata High School
Tani

00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:41.640
The swallow.

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:42.640
Correct.

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:45.350
In "CV," the abbreviation 
used for anime voice actors,

00:16:45.350 --> 00:16:48.360
"C" stands for "character," and "V—

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:49.170
Voice!

00:16:49.450 --> 00:16:50.400
Correct!

00:16:51.630 --> 00:16:52.700
Wrap.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:53.710
Correct!

00:16:53.070 --> 00:16:56.370
Sekigawata High School 
Tani

00:16:53.710 --> 00:16:56.370
Tani-kun of Sekigawata High 
School passes the round!

00:16:56.770 --> 00:16:58.230
<i>Only one left.</i>

00:16:58.590 --> 00:17:00.370
<i>Even Inoue's been able to buzz in.</i>

00:17:01.010 --> 00:17:03.240
<i>Maybe I really can't do this.</i>

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:05.490
<i>I couldn't even do the buzzer test right,</i>

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:08.840
<i>and I don't know what the 
classic questions are.</i>

00:17:09.170 --> 00:17:10.800
<i>Don't give up!</i>

00:17:11.060 --> 00:17:11.840
Question.

00:17:12.310 --> 00:17:16.130
The "Shiki" of "Masaoka Shiki" means 
"lesser cuckoo," and "Ishikawa—

00:17:16.870 --> 00:17:17.740
<i>Literature...</i>

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:21.660
<i>The only writer named Ishikawa who could 
compare to Masaoka Shiki is Ishikawa Takuboku.</i>

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:22.700
<i>If it's "Takuboku"...</i>

00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:23.850
Woodpecker.

00:17:24.110 --> 00:17:24.640
Yes!

00:17:24.640 --> 00:17:25.310
Correct!

00:17:25.550 --> 00:17:26.230
Question.

00:17:26.640 --> 00:17:29.270
"Man is a thinking reed" is a—

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:30.990
<i>A quote!</i>

00:17:31.500 --> 00:17:32.030
Pascal!

00:17:32.690 --> 00:17:33.490
Correct!

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:36.620
<i>That's right! There are 
subjects I excel in, too!</i>

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:40.060
The high-fat food known as 
"butter of the forest"—

00:17:41.270 --> 00:17:42.410
Avocado.

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:43.330
Correct!

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:45.830
This is a close battle.

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:47.840
Both players are within 
one point of advancing,

00:17:47.840 --> 00:17:49.790
and only one spot remains!

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:50.970
Question.

00:17:50.970 --> 00:17:55.130
Hiraoka Kimitake is the real name 
of <i>The Temple of the Golden</i>—

00:17:57.280 --> 00:18:02.060
Five, four, three, two, one.

00:18:03.360 --> 00:18:06.100
The correct answer is Mishima Yukio.

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:06.100
<b>Hiraoka Kimitake is the real name of <i>The 
Temple of the Golden</i>" author known by what pen name?</b>

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:08.230
Looks like you're saved, Koshiyama.

00:18:08.590 --> 00:18:09.910
That's as it should be.

00:18:10.760 --> 00:18:13.450
We're the ones who were saved.

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:17.300
She didn't get the right answer, 
but she stopped him from answering,

00:18:17.300 --> 00:18:18.540
so it worked out.

00:18:19.820 --> 00:18:21.790
<i>How was I beaten out on 
a literature question?</i>

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:23.840
<i>I knew that one, too!</i>

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:25.770
<i>If that was a classic...</i>

00:18:25.770 --> 00:18:29.170
<i>No, classics mean nothing! 
Don't let classics beat me!</i>

00:18:29.350 --> 00:18:30.700
<i>I can't win if I don't buzz!</i>

00:18:30.700 --> 00:18:32.310
<i>Just one more point!</i>

00:18:33.430 --> 00:18:34.000
Question.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:35.640
<i>I just have to buzz in!</i>

00:18:35.640 --> 00:18:36.710
A miniskirt—

00:18:37.830 --> 00:18:39.590
<i>I pushed down too far!</i>

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:45.680
<i>What about a miniskirt? What am I 
supposed to get from that one word?</i>

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:47.640
<i>What are you doing, Koshiyama-kun?</i>

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:49.560
<i>Even if you don't know, just say something!</i>

00:18:50.100 --> 00:18:52.350
<i>Minisk... Miniskirt...</i>

00:18:52.350 --> 00:18:54.530
<i>Fukami-san... Mini...</i>

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:56.020
<i>It doesn't even matter!</i>

00:18:56.020 --> 00:18:58.060
<i>Whether I answer or not, it'll end the same!</i>

00:18:58.060 --> 00:19:01.280
<i>No, if I don't answer, 
I don't even have a chance!</i>

00:19:01.280 --> 00:19:02.180
<i>Zero chance!</i>

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:05.240
<i>Absolute territory!</i>

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:08.540
Yeah, right.

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:12.280
Correct!

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:15.000
Koshiyama-kun of Buzou High 
School passes the round!

00:19:15.740 --> 00:19:19.180
A miniskirt, worn with knee-high socks,

00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:23.690
leaves a patch of the thighs visible 
in a "moe" slang term known as what?

00:19:23.690 --> 00:19:25.880
The answer is "absolute territory"!

00:19:26.090 --> 00:19:27.390
Unbelievable...

00:19:27.820 --> 00:19:29.040
Those happen sometimes.

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:32.610
Humorous questions that would only 
come up between students or insiders.

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:35.520
You drew the question itself 
toward you, Koshiyama-kun!

00:19:35.520 --> 00:19:36.800
You're...

00:19:38.700 --> 00:19:42.230
Quiz bowl is a lot more 
stressful than I thought...

00:19:43.400 --> 00:19:44.340
Koshiyama?!

00:19:45.020 --> 00:19:47.870
We will now take a lunch break.

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:49.620
Ladies'
Restroom
for
Visitors

00:19:54.350 --> 00:19:55.040
Maririn...

00:19:59.210 --> 00:20:00.760
Do you enjoy quiz bowl, Yukicchi?

00:20:01.980 --> 00:20:03.180
What do you mean?

00:20:04.180 --> 00:20:09.390
I mean, you got into quiz 
bowl because of me, right?

00:20:11.850 --> 00:20:15.360
I do enjoy it. Enough that 
I joined the team by myself.

00:20:16.340 --> 00:20:17.660
Yukicchi...

00:20:18.520 --> 00:20:19.820
I'm so glad!

00:20:27.510 --> 00:20:28.490
You okay?

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:30.580
You were amazing, Koshiyama-kun.

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:34.630
There aren't many beginners 
who can stay that focused.

00:20:35.490 --> 00:20:36.630
Y-Yeah...

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:39.100
Here. Have something sweet.

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:41.420
When your brain is fatigued, you need sugar.

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:43.760
Th-Tha... Thanks.

00:20:44.990 --> 00:20:47.390
<i>I got chocolate from a girl...</i>

00:20:48.250 --> 00:20:51.340
<i>I was right. You're exactly 
what I thought you were.</i>

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:56.810
<i>I'm sure you'll be able to show that 
power even more in the next round.</i>

00:22:31.050 --> 00:22:32.280
The "determining point" is

00:22:32.280 --> 00:22:35.000
the point in a question at which 
you can determine the answer,

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:37.680
which dictates when you 
should press the buzzer.

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:38.750
<b>Determining Point</b>

00:22:37.680 --> 00:22:38.750
Got that?

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:40.250
Y-Yes!

00:22:40.590 --> 00:22:42.380
It's hard when you're not used to it,

00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:44.930
but it's an absolutely essential 
technique for fast buzz-ins!

00:22:45.620 --> 00:22:47.520
Now, let's put it into practice.

00:22:47.890 --> 00:22:48.720
Question.

00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:51.380
After stripes, Fukami-kun's preferred—

00:22:48.760 --> 00:22:51.010
<b>After stripes,
Fukami-kun's preferred—</b>

00:22:51.260 --> 00:22:52.010
<b>Polka-dots</b>

00:22:51.380 --> 00:22:52.010
Polka-dots.

00:22:52.310 --> 00:22:54.520
Correct! I knew you'd get it, Sasajima-kun!

00:22:54.790 --> 00:22:58.020
Hey! What did you even determine from that?!

00:22:58.330 --> 00:22:59.580
<i>Polka-dots?</i>
